 "title": "What Matters More Than Salary",
 "topic": "mindset",
 "summary": "The creator explains that before negotiating a salary, you should negotiate your role and growth. He suggests evaluating how your work impacts the company's revenue, cost, or customer experience, and whether the job pushes you out of your comfort zone.",
 "key_points": [
  "Negotiate your role and the scope of your role first.",
  "Check if your role touches increasing revenue, reducing cost, or improving customer experience (or more than one).",
  "Assess whether you will learn fast and grow fast in terms of the tasks you have to do.",
  "Evaluate whether the role will push you outside of your comfort zone."
 ],
 "content": "Post text: Before Negotiating Your Salary, Negotiate Your Growth. 🚀💼 Ankit Agarwal shares an important lesson for anyone choosing a job: don't make salary your only priority. First, understand your role, its scope, and how much impact you'll have on the company. Ask yourself whether your work will help increase revenue, reduce costs, or improve customer experience. These are the areas where businesses create real value. More importantly, will the role push you outside your comfort zone? Will you learn new skills, take on bigger responsibilities, and grow faster professionally? A job that challenges you can help build the skills and experience that create better opportunities in the future. Don't just negotiate for a bigger paycheck today. Choose a role that makes you more valuable tomorrow. 💯 Featured: Ankit Agarwal | Think School Podcast #CareerGrowth #SalaryNegotiation #CareerAdvice #ProfessionalGrowth #ThinkSchool Transcript: I think the first thing that you should be negotiating on is ki [what] what is my role? What is the scope of my role? How important is this to the company? Is it touching one of those three things: increasing revenue, reducing cost, or improving customer experience? Or more than one? Will I learn fast? Will I grow fast? Not in salary, but in terms of things that I have to do. Will I be outside of my comfort zone? On screen text: WHAT MATTERS MORE THAN SALARY? Choose Growth First",
